'' T70: TIKO_LIBPATH NAMING THE TARGET'S OWN DIRECTORY BRINGS ITS '-fb' SIBLING, as the
'' bundled tree does, and so fbrt0.o. 'TIKO_LIBPATH=lib/linux-x86_64' alone linked no
'' fbrt0.o: fb_hRtInit and fb_hRtExit never ran, and a runtime error's "Aborting due
'' to runtime error" never reached stderr -- measured on Linux, and silent.
'' SINCE 2026-10-10 THE OBJECT IS TIKO-RT'S OWN (lib/rt/src/c/fbrt0.c), packaged beside
'' libfb.a in lib/win64/, and the -fb directory no longer carries fbc's.
'' SKIPPED since 2026-10-10: -target win64 (the MinGW ABI) is no longer packaged, so the
'' toolchain this links against has no lib/win64. The compiler still has the target; to
'' run this, build tiko-rt for it (lib/rt/build/build.sh Release win64), point the paths
'' below at lib/rt/lib/win64, and set TEST back to cli.
'' TEST: skip
'' ARGS: -v -target win64 tests/driver/src/mt-startup.bas -o tests/driver/libpathfb.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: win64/fbrt0.o
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/libpathfb.exe
